              %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_43.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_44.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi BV
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BV_\infty
            and
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_45.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi HyperComm
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HyperComm_\infty
          %blockquote
            %p (was hard to take typed notes of this otherwise pretty cool talk, does anyone have handwriitten notes?)
          %h2#scott_wilson_categorical_algebra_mapping_spaces_and_applications Scott Wilson: Categorical algebra, mapping spaces and applications
          %p (for closely related blog entry see
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2008/04/higher_hochschild_cohomology_a.html"} Higher Hochschild Cohomology and Differential Forms on Mapping Spaces
          %p )
          %p outline
          %ul
            %li
              %p language for some elementary algebraic topology
            %li
              %p application to generalizatons of Hochschild complexes
            %li
              %p Examples
              %ul
                %li
                  %p invariants on mapping spaces
                %li
                  %p contributions related to def of Laplacian
          %p
            %strong def/lema
          %p
            A commutative associative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded+algebra"} differential graded algebra
            is (equivalently given by) a strict monoidal functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_46.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi FinSet
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ChainComplexes
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (FinSet, \coprod) \to (ChainComplexes, \otimes)
          %p generalize this
          %p
            %strong def
            a
            %strong partial DGA
            is a monoidal functor with coherence map given by weak equivalence in the model structure
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_47.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi FinSet
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ChainComplexes
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A :  (FinSet, \coprod) \to (ChainComplexes, \otimes)
          %p i.e. there exists a natural weak equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_48.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo ⊔
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A(j \sqcup k) \stackrel{T}{\to} A(j) \otimes A(k)
          %p that respects the obvious coherence properties
          %p generalized
          %ul
            %li
              %p 1) co-algebras
            %li
              %p 2) any operad
            %li
              %p
                3) note that
                %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_49.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi FinSet
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet_*
                (pointed finite sets) is a module over
                = succeed "," do
                  %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_50.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi FinSet
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet
          %p
            Then weak partial algebras can be functorially replaced by
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_51.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
          %p
            %strong example
          %p
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_52.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a space
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_53.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \stackrel{f}{\to} k
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_54.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi j
                  %mo =
                  %mi Map
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ←
                  %mi Map
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X^j = Map(j,X) \leftarrow Map(k,X) = X^k
          %p pass to the chains version of this
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_55.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ←
                  %msub
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ch_*(X^j) \leftarrow Ch_*(X^k)
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_56.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ch^*(X^j) \to Ch^*(X^k)
          %p by Kuenneth formula we have a chain equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_57.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo +
                      %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C_*(X^j) \otimes C_*(X^k) \to C_*(X^{j+k})
          %p and similarly for cochains.
          %p so this gives two things:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a partial coalgebra on
                %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_58.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_*(X)
            %li
              %p
                a partial algebra on
                %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_59.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*(X)
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_60.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            be any finite simplicial space. A partial algebra
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_61.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} gama
                  %mi FinSet
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %mi ChainCompl
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta \stackrel{\gama}{\to} FinSet \stackrel{A}{\to} ChainCompl
          %p
            simplicial object in
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_62.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ChainCompl
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ChainCompl
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_63.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi CH
                    %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CH^\gamma(A)
          %p meaning generalization of Hochschild complex
          %ul
            %li this is joint work with Tradler and Zanelli (spelling? probably wrong)
          %p goes back to Pitashvili and more recently Gregory Ginot
          %p
            For
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_64.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \Omega(X)
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_65.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi CH
                    %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CH^\gamma(A)
            computes cohomology of
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_66.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\gamma
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_67.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is sufficiently connected
          %p
            %strong example
          %p
            let
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_68.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a strict algebra, and
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_69.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mo =
                  %mi Y
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma = Y = S^1
            then
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_70.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi CH
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CH^{S^1}(A) = \prod_{n \geq 0} A \otimes A^{\otimes n}
          %p is the Hochschild complex
          %p there is also a shuffle product in the game, so this implies there is an exponential map
          %p calculate:
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_71.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(| \otimes x)
                  \=
                  | + | \otimes x + | \otimes  x \otimes x + | \otimes  x \otimes x \otimes x + \cdots +
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_72.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi d
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  D \exp(1 \otimes x) = (1 \otimes d x + x \cdot x) \cdot e^{1 \otimes x}
          %p
            then: if
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_73.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d x + x \cdot x = 0
            then
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_74.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D e^{1 \otimes x} = 0
          %p this reminds us of curvature and connection
          %p this can be taken further
          %p
            let
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_75.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \Omega^\bullet(M)
            be differential forms on
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_76.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_77.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi CH
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi S
                                %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi M
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi S
                                %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi M
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi ch
                        %mtd
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi M
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; CH^{S^1}(A) (\simeq \Omega(M^{S^1}))
                  \\\
                  \&amp;\nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  K(M)&amp;\stackrel{ch}{\to}&amp;\Omega(M)
                  }
          %p commutes (due to some people)
          %p
            %strong example 2
          %p
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_78.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo =
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y = I
            (the interval)
          %p
            then
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_79.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi CH
                    %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CH^I(A)
            is the 2-sided bar construction
          %p
            more generally
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_80.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CH
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %mi M
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi n
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CH(A, M, N) = \prod_{n \geq 0} M \otimes A^{\otimes n} \otimes N
          %p
            with
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_81.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            and
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_82.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_83.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            consider the case
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_84.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Riemannian
                  %mi manifold
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \Omega^\bullet(Riemannian manifold)
            and
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_85.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo =
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M = A
            and
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_86.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo .
                  %mo .
                  %mo .
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi d
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = (\Omega^\bullet(...), d^* , (x\in A) \cdot (y\in N) = \star^{-1}(x \wedge \star y)))
          %p
            (the operatoin on
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_87.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            here is the intersection product of forms)
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_88.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            be differential on
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_89.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi CH
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CH^I
          %p
            let
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_90.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            be differential on
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_91.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi CH
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CH^I
            for normal structure, and and
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_92.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^*
            for
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_93.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, M, N
            as just described.
          %p Set
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_94.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta = [D, D^*]
          %p
            then acting with this
            %math#mathml_9bb44436969d5121ebd35a6fcdb5b6ac034e70f0_95.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            on something produces interesting non-linear differential equations related to Witten’t Morse-theory deformation of susy quantum mechanics and to Navier-Stokes’ equations in fluid dynamics…
